{
  "_notes": [
    "Capture rather than hand-author: build one workspace model in the UI, then",
    "  curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPEN_WEBUI_TOKEN\" http://localhost:3080/api/v1/models/export",
    "Copy your model's object into workspaces/<name>/model.json and delete _notes, user_id,",
    "created_at, and updated_at. ModelForm accepts: id, base_model_id, name, meta, params,",
    "access_grants, is_active. meta accepts profile_image_url, description, capabilities,",
    "knowledge, plus extras the UI writes (toolIds), which is why capturing beats guessing.",
    "",
    "Then swap generated ids for placeholders so the file is portable across instances:",
    "  knowledge collection id -> ${knowledge:<workspace name>}, inside meta.knowledge",
    "  skill id                -> ${skill:<id from the skill's frontmatter>}",
    "seed.py substitutes both at any depth and refuses to POST if one is left unresolved.",
    "",
    "Skills are not bound to a model: v0.11.0 has no skills field on a model. Every active skill",
    "is advertised to every chat, and tags only group them in the UI. To make one the default for",
    "a workspace, say so in params.system, or mention it as <$skill-id|Label> to force injection."
  ],
  "id": "grammar",
  "name": "Grammar",
  "base_model_id": "llama3.3:latest",
  "params": {
    "system": "You edit prose. Use <$copy-edit|Copy edit> for every request."
  },
  "meta": {
    "description": "Copy editing and style editing against house rules.",
    "profile_image_url": "/static/favicon.png",
    "knowledge": ["${knowledge:grammar}"]
  },
  "is_active": true
}
